WEBVTT

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:07.580
I found their hideout. 
It was just around the corner.

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:11.780
I was being a fool, desperately searching for this place.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.480
I know he'll definitely be here.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:20.380
I'm not going to lose him this time.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.210
I'm hungry. I'm going to eat something.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.050
Hello this is Cafe Hakobune.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:33.510
Hey, it's me. I want to place an order.

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:36.210
I want one ramen with extra sungan.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:38.600
One ramen. Right away, sir!

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:42.870
I have an order for delivery, Kanako.

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:47.810
Let's get right on it, Yayoi. 
What is that dish called?

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:52.490
I--- I forgot the name of the dish.

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:54.880
Can you tell me what kind of dish it is?

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:56.950
I sure will.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:00.330
It was the most delightful menu.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:05.140
Inside the serene salt, the noodles are full like wave-like waterways.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:09.790
The whirlpool swallows the logs floating on the surface.

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:14.690
Reminds me of the Sea of Setouchi, tranquil and boisterous.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:18.290
And there, lies the two attractive slices of meat.

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:21.220
Covering this masterpiece of nature...

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:24.820
...the people are moved and anticipate more.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.880
Wow what a wonderful dish!

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:31.100
Have you heard of such a dish?

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.580
Yes, of course I have.

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:41.420
I'm making my delivery from Cafe Hakobune!

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:44.540
Ohh, it's here! 
I've been waiting!

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:47.120
Thanks for the wait. 
Here it is!

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:52.980
I thought I ordered a ramen.

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:28.720
Lonely Tropical Fish

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:35.810
- So heavy. 
-Maybe, I bought too much.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:39.660
Event though it was a sale, you've bought too much.

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:43.900
You weakling! 
Go work out!

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:46.670
You're going to have problems later.

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:49.410
What do you mean later?

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:52.750
Like when you need to protect your loved one.

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:54.980
I don't care.

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:57.600
I'll be single forever.

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:01.830
You're useless, give me one.

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:08.230
- Thanks. 
- You'll never be able to  live on your own like this.

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:09.410
Well, excuse me.

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:11.550
Hey...

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:12.660
Yeah?

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:16.200
You talked about protecting your loved one. 
Are you talking about Arashi-san?

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:19.510
- Of course, she comes first! 
- Comes first?

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:24.070
Your loved one is not always only one person. 
Say like, my grandpa.

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:27.950
Of course everyone at Hakobune. 
That includes you.

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:32.630
- Me too? 
- Well, you're closer to the bottom in priority.

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:38.110
We're back!

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:43.620
- What's the matter, Arashi-san? 
- Master said she has an important announcement.

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:46.750
Well, it's about this.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:50.730
- What is that? 
- Raw oysters that I bought as snacks for my drink.

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:53.500
The expiration date is a month ago.

00:04:54.010 --> 00:04:59.200
- Are you telling us to?! 
- Yes! Bring this back before the expiration by time traveling.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:02.670
- I'm not responsible for this! 
- Come on, don't say that.

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:05.410
It's your fault for not eating it before it expired.

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:09.590
I was saving the best for last, but I totally forgot about it.

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:13.760
- If it's so important to you, why did you forget? 
- I was drinking! Of course I'll forget!

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:16.560
It's your bad for leaving raw foods last.

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:19.940
Such a waste. 
Can't you do something about it?

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:24.300
- Seriously, oysters are dangerous, oysters are!
- But, it's from Kesennuma.

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:27.230
- It doesn't matter! 
- It's natural oysters.

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:31.500
- It doesn't matter! 
- My gosh, you're badly brought up.

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:34.300
- Why would you throw food away? 
- It's my fault?

00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:38.830
What am I supposed to do? 
Am I supposed to drink without snacks?

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:41.690
When will she ever learn?

00:05:41.790 --> 00:05:46.090
Even if we take it in the past, it won't be fresh again.

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:48.260
What's wrong, Yayoi?

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:52.880
If we place it in the past, more time will add on, right?

00:05:57.530 --> 00:05:59.340
Yayoi-chan, what's that?

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:02.850
It's pickled cabbage.  I just made it right now.

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:06.030
Hajime-san, can you come along with me?

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:07.310
Sure!

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:20.650
Where the hell did they go?

00:06:22.850 --> 00:06:25.140
- I'm back! 
- We're back!

00:06:25.430 --> 00:06:29.130
- Yayoi-san, where are the pickles? 
- They're up in the attic.

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:30.430
Huh?

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:34.600
Oh, there it is!

00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:37.950
The pickle barrel from earlier.

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:45.560
Look, the cabbage pickled this morning is delicious!

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:47.980
This is perfect for my beer!

00:06:47.980 --> 00:06:52.670
I went back three days ago and hid it where no one can find it.

00:06:52.730 --> 00:06:56.170
So, the cabbage is now pickled for three days.

00:06:56.490 --> 00:07:00.570
Wow, is this the so called, "Time Paradox?"

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:03.400
No, that's pickled cabbage.

00:07:03.910 --> 00:07:09.800
Then how's this? 
It's Nukadocollins that I got from Nukadokolina.

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:12.450
I just pickled some eggplants.

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:14.100
Alright, I'm going!

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:26.810
- How was it? 
- I went to half a day before.

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:30.410
Oh, there's Nukadocollins.

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:36.970
Amazing! 
A light-pickled eggplant just like that!

00:07:37.070 --> 00:07:41.050
- These are great for my beer! 
- We resolved your snack issue.

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:43.470
You're going to drink in the morning?

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:48.440
I see. 
The point is to hide it so no one can find it.

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:54.720
As long as you don't notice it now, you won't notice it in the past either.

00:07:55.610 --> 00:07:59.910
Hey, then how's this? 
The clothes that are wet right now will be dry, don't you think?

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:01.910
Arashi-san, I'll go with you!

00:08:06.440 --> 00:08:08.510
- How was it? 
- Here's the result.

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:15.200
I've put it in the refrigerator this morning. 
Look, it feels so cold.

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:17.460
But it's not dry.

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:22.810
- Of course! 
- Why in the fridge?

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:26.920
Because we couldn't think of any other place!

00:08:28.390 --> 00:08:32.690
- It smells like rags! 
- These have to be washed again.

00:08:32.850 --> 00:08:36.130
Oh well, at least it'll feel cool.

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:38.520
You're right! 
Hajime-chan.

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:42.370
- Here, put these on. 
- Ohh, it's so cold, and it smells.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:47.120
- Come on, try these on! 
- Oh please forgive me!

00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:49.120
No also means yes!

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:53.580
- Here, while it's still cold. 
- Ugh, it stinks.

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:05.910
- You two sure get along great. 
- What do you mean "you two?"

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:10.050
You and Arashi-san. 
How's it going recently?

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:13.170
What's up? You ask me out of the blue.

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:17.030
- Hey. 
- Ouch, don't hit me so hard!

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:22.090
So you want to know. 
Alright, then I'll tell you.

00:09:23.270 --> 00:09:27.320
The relationship betweeen Arashi-san and I is healthy. 
As a matter of fact, it's excellent!

00:09:27.640 --> 00:09:30.920
Last time, we went to the Parasite Museum together!

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:35.850
There were so many displays that looked like maggots!

00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:41.240
There's an 8.8 meter tapeworm display that looked like a long udon!

00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:44.420
I can't believe those things live in the stomach!

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:47.670
- What's wrong, Jun? 
- Um.

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:51.430
Anyhow, the one and only Parasite Museum.

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:56.720
- Arashi-san and I got so excited! Overwhelmed! 
- Lame.

00:09:57.870 --> 00:10:03.440
- What the hell, you asked me first! 
- You think a girl would have fun there?

00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:09.680
Do you seriously love Arashi-san?

00:10:10.890 --> 00:10:16.690
<i>- Make sure you fall in love!</i> 
- It's not just an infatuation?

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:20.040
<i>We've lost our lives already.</i>

00:10:20.480 --> 00:10:23.220
- Do you really love her? 
- Yup!

00:10:23.410 --> 00:10:25.900
<i>I'll be gone once summer is over.</i>

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:31.690
<i>Having a relationship in that situation, it's wistful.</i>

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:37.680
- I see. 
- Hey what's the matter, you look so serious.

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:42.680
- What's up all of the sudden? 
- No, it's nothing.

00:10:43.130 --> 00:10:45.260
<i>She said she never fell in love before.</i>

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:49.370
<i>Even after living for 60 years, she remains a young girl.</i>

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:53.770
<i>But she's so happy. 
I don't feel like falling in love right now.</i>

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:56.000
<i>I can live on like that.</i>

00:10:56.350 --> 00:11:00.710
<i>But not Arashi-san. 
Even if she wanted to fall in love, she couldn't.</i>

00:11:03.450 --> 00:11:07.560
<i>Isn't that something that's hard for her to accept?</i>

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:13.520
Hey, instead of going to your bizarre dates.

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:18.230
- Have you asked her out as a man? 
- No need for that.

00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:22.410
Since I'm always 100% serious!

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:27.380
Besides, Arashi-san doesn't measure her happiness from the location of the dates.

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:33.460
<i>I'm surprised. 
He's pretty serious.</i>

00:11:35.150 --> 00:11:39.390
Arashi-san. 
Would you like to go to the movies with me sometime?

00:11:39.390 --> 00:11:40.050
What?

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:42.070
May I get some sa--

00:11:48.110 --> 00:11:49.230
- To the movies? 
- Salt!

00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:52.090
I thought it'll be nice for once.

00:11:52.570 --> 00:11:55.090
How great! 
What are we watching?

00:11:55.280 --> 00:11:57.410
- Arashi-san, what kind of movies do you like? 
- Hey, Yasaka.

00:11:57.410 --> 00:11:59.990
- Well, anything with colors. 
- Don't worry about it.

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:00.470
But.

00:12:00.470 --> 00:12:04.040
- It'll be nice if it had sound too! 
- Color? Sound?

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:08.020
I want to watch something funny. 
 Something like <i>Raccoon dog Palaces</i>!

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:09.740
- Raccoon? 
- Dokkoi!

00:12:09.970 --> 00:12:14.300
- Arashi, what are you doing during work? 
- Oh, sorry.

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:16.370
I think it's okay.

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:19.590
They say, if you disturb other people's love life you won't live long.

00:12:19.780 --> 00:12:24.460
Times have changed. 
Picking up girls in this broad daylight.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:29.300
- Don't watch this Yayoi, it's a bad influence. 
- Oh, but.

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:31.820
Arashi-san, what time are you done today?

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:36.050
- Hey Yamashiro, why do you speak in honorifics to Arashi and the others? 
- Huh?

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:41.180
Don't you feel like a dirty old man talking to high school girls?

00:12:42.300 --> 00:12:47.460
No, don't you feel like Arashi-san and the others are older? 
Check!

00:12:52.110 --> 00:12:56.500
My, Yamashiro-san. 
Does that mean that I'm like an old lady?

00:12:57.590 --> 00:12:58.420
I'm joking.

00:12:58.990 --> 00:13:00.900
Sounds eerie.

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:03.070
But, I think it's weird too.

00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:07.180
I usually like older women, but why?

00:13:09.050 --> 00:13:13.830
Hey, Yamashiro-san. 
Is it true that you like older women?

00:13:14.180 --> 00:13:19.020
- Who was talking about you? 
- Kaya, is that guy safe?

00:13:19.220 --> 00:13:22.970
Kanako-san! 
Do we look that old already?

00:13:23.420 --> 00:13:29.000
You shall suffer by fighting against time. 
That is the universal law.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:34.090
People have their own preference, do whatever you like.

00:13:36.230 --> 00:13:36.900
Ouch!

00:13:37.180 --> 00:13:40.780
Then Arashi-san, after you're done I'll pick you up.

00:13:40.780 --> 00:13:44.480
- Huh? 
- See you later, checkmate.

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:49.160
Thank you!

00:13:53.650 --> 00:13:59.420
- Are you sure, Yasaka? 
- Huh, man shall wait in confidence.

00:13:59.930 --> 00:14:03.460
- But. 
- Arashi-san and I are "connected."

00:14:03.650 --> 00:14:06.770
Is there a deeper connection than that? 
Huh?

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:10.280
- Yasaka. 
- Huh?

00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:13.430
No, never mind.

00:14:13.430 --> 00:14:18.370
Hey, I don't like that. 
If you're a man, be clear with your words.

00:14:18.660 --> 00:14:21.110
Yasaka, can we talk for a minute?

00:14:24.200 --> 00:14:29.010
- Arashi-san never told you? 
- About what?

00:14:29.900 --> 00:14:34.200
Arashi-san, after the summer is over, Arashi-san...

00:14:48.630 --> 00:14:50.760
<i>What did you say right now?</i>

00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:52.070
<i>May I get some salt...</i>

00:14:55.130 --> 00:14:56.470
<i>What!</i>

00:14:58.060 --> 00:14:59.400
Yay!

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:07.230
That was so fun! 
It was my first time playing darts.

00:15:07.520 --> 00:15:10.450
I didn't know that was the popular thing to do now days.

00:15:11.920 --> 00:15:15.610
Now days? 
You sure don't sound like you're in high school.

00:15:16.820 --> 00:15:21.730
But, that comforts me. 
I'm not really good with girls that are too trendy.

00:15:21.950 --> 00:15:26.380
It might be because my parents were strict. 
It comforts me talking to you.

00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:34.600
You have class and you're calm.

00:15:34.820 --> 00:15:37.750
I can understand those things well.

00:15:39.630 --> 00:15:45.010
- Oh, don't make me blush! 
- It's true, though you don't speak much.

00:15:46.190 --> 00:15:49.470
I don't know where you were born and where you're from.

00:15:49.540 --> 00:15:54.760
I'll tell you about it when the time is right.

00:15:55.590 --> 00:15:59.380
I hope that time comes soon. 
Can I wait for that time?

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:02.560
I'm embarrassed!

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:06.710
- Sorry to embarrass you, let's go now. 
- OK!

00:16:07.950 --> 00:16:08.650
I'm home!

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:13.270
It's late! 
Where the hell were you?!

00:16:13.270 --> 00:16:17.950
- Do you like that pretty boy that much? 
- Alright. Alright.

00:16:18.970 --> 00:16:22.280
- As punishment, go on a date with me too! 
- What?

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:26.360
- So it's like that? 
- We're going, come on!

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:34.230
Once the summer is over, Arashi-san will...

00:16:36.580 --> 00:16:39.040
...be gone!

00:16:40.440 --> 00:16:43.370
<i>Should I ask her about what Jun told me?</i>

00:16:43.820 --> 00:16:46.140
<i>No, that's not what's important.</i>

00:16:46.430 --> 00:16:51.460
<i>Even if Arashi-san is gone. 
Even if I can't prevent it.</i>

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:55.860
<i>Even if I don't have the wings to chase her. 
Who cares?!</i>

00:16:57.000 --> 00:17:02.260
It's about if I can still love Arashi-san. 
That's nonsense!

00:17:03.020 --> 00:17:05.440
<i>My answer has always been definite.</i>

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:11.430
- Arashi-san, Jun told me. 
- Is that so.

00:17:12.100 --> 00:17:16.020
- Is it true that you'll be gone once the summer is over? 
- Yes.

00:17:16.820 --> 00:17:17.870
What about next year?

00:17:18.700 --> 00:17:21.720
I don't think we'll meet next year.

00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:25.070
Why? 
Won't you be at Hakobune every year?

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:26.660
Yea---

00:17:27.550 --> 00:17:31.210
Then all I have to do is come to Hakobune next year.

00:17:31.790 --> 00:17:37.430
- I don't think you'll come next year. 
- Why? I'll definitely come

00:17:38.350 --> 00:17:41.760
Even if you see me next year, you wouldn't recognize me.

00:17:42.270 --> 00:17:46.890
Why? 
Do I lose my memory from time traveling?

00:17:47.680 --> 00:17:51.380
That's not it, how should I put it.

00:17:51.950 --> 00:17:55.200
It's a little complicated, but Hajime-chan...

00:17:55.460 --> 00:17:57.110
..no matter how special it is...

00:17:57.560 --> 00:18:03.320
... unrealistic experiences like this are going to be overwhelmed by real ones later.

00:18:03.320 --> 00:18:05.490
And you'll stop believing in them.

00:18:07.370 --> 00:18:09.850
Like a dream, like a fantasy.

00:18:10.300 --> 00:18:14.570
Like an obscure child's misconception, it'll later be forgotten.

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:18.800
That's the truth about becoming an adult for everyone.

00:18:19.060 --> 00:18:19.860
But, I'll...

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:23.740
Will become an adult. Everyone does.

00:18:24.980 --> 00:18:25.620
So.

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:28.420
I will never forget.

00:18:28.680 --> 00:18:32.470
No matter what, I will never forget about you!

00:18:33.140 --> 00:18:38.040
Someone said that to me before. 
But, that's why.

00:18:40.660 --> 00:18:42.660
Arashi-san!

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:47.190
I love Arashi-san! 
I'm serious!

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:51.100
- Hajime-chan. 
- Arashi-san, will you...

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:54.190
Sorry, Hajime-chan.

00:18:56.390 --> 00:18:58.970
I can't, anymore... 
I'm sorry.

00:19:23.880 --> 00:19:26.210
Guys having feelings for me...

00:19:26.780 --> 00:19:28.670
...it's like being tickled.

00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:30.410
It startles me.

00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:37.040
But, before realizing that it's love.

00:19:37.390 --> 00:19:41.400
Even if it was love, it'll all be gone at the end of summer.

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:44.870
I'm like a cicada.

00:19:45.510 --> 00:19:49.840
If I truly fall in love, my heart will wrench in suffering. 
It'll make me crazy.

00:19:50.320 --> 00:19:54.050
I'll cry a river because I'll miss him so much.

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:57.170
Even if I want them, they'll forget me.

00:19:57.780 --> 00:20:00.460
Even if I wait forever, I won't ever see him.

00:20:00.740 --> 00:20:04.310
I will live with suffering forever.

00:20:04.560 --> 00:20:09.120
And I'll just continue in my death.

00:20:21.860 --> 00:20:24.410
Welcome! 
Please have the seats in the back.

00:20:26.320 --> 00:20:28.000
- Yasaka? 
- What?

00:20:28.260 --> 00:20:31.760
No, just wondering what happened after that.

00:20:31.760 --> 00:20:35.040
- Nothing in particular. Why? 
- Nothing.

00:20:35.430 --> 00:20:38.740
- Hajime-chan, one iced coffee please! 
- OK!

00:20:43.490 --> 00:20:46.000
What's wrong Kamigamo? You're just sitting there.

00:20:46.380 --> 00:20:47.750
No, nothing.

00:20:47.750 --> 00:20:52.210
- Huh!? 
- What's the matter, Master?

00:20:52.210 --> 00:20:56.130
I was about to make sake-steamed clams for my beer.

00:20:56.230 --> 00:20:57.820
But I forgot to get the sand out.

00:20:58.010 --> 00:20:58.680
No!

00:20:58.680 --> 00:21:01.010
Drinking in the morning, again?

00:21:01.010 --> 00:21:03.970
I was trying to eat it before I forget it.

00:21:03.970 --> 00:21:06.680
Is not drinking one of your options?

00:21:06.680 --> 00:21:09.320
It's not good unless you make them spit the sand out.

00:21:09.960 --> 00:21:15.880
Oh yeah, you guys take it back to yesterday. 
It'll be fine after one day.

00:21:15.950 --> 00:21:21.040
- Time traveling again? 
- Time consuming dishes can be made in a flash!

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:26.430
- So useful! 
- Superpowers are being used for cooking.

00:21:29.040 --> 00:21:32.610
- Can't help it. 
- Let's go Arashi-san!

00:21:39.040 --> 00:21:41.330
- Huh? 
- What was that?

00:21:49.970 --> 00:21:52.070
- Hajime-chan. 
- Arashi-san.

00:21:52.670 --> 00:21:54.940
Oh my god, you guys.

00:21:56.430 --> 00:21:57.740
I can't fly anymore.

00:21:57.740 --> 00:21:59.330
What?!

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:32.190
Let's talk about dates.

00:23:32.280 --> 00:23:33.840
Kaya-san, will you pay for your own dinner?

00:23:33.840 --> 00:23:38.490
I feel bad about getting treated. 
But, wouldn't that be presumptuous?

00:23:38.520 --> 00:23:40.210
Kaya-san, have you ever gone on a date before?

00:23:40.210 --> 00:23:43.620
Huh? Uhh, umm. 
Tomorrow is another day!
